{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/fixtures/go/auth.go@L8","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/fixtures/go/auth.go","span":{"start":8,"end":8}},"file":"packages/parsers/fixtures/go/auth.go","span":{"start":8,"end":8},"lang":"go","hash":"blake3:c27f58a3fac699597f05ad5be7a390066f0803466a8a2bc16feabd8e3f18b8d0","meta":{"text":"Auth controller: login + token issuance."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts@L117","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":117,"end":131}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":117,"end":131},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:1f99ce3033fe0f69ef0691a539969ebd99c9b336edd6fa8b719454aeecf31e1a","meta":{"text":"Phase 2: run the registry over every file, persisting nodes + intra-file edges to the soul.\nPARALLEL MODES (M3.4):\n- `concurrency` (default, when `parallel !== false`): bounded async pool — overlaps readFile I/O\non the event loop, persists in discovery order. ~1.2-1.3× measured, deterministic, no workers.\n- `workers` (opt-in via `KCRIB_PARALLEL=workers`, default fleet only): worker-thread pool. Net-\nnegative for crib's small-file workload (cold-JIT + clone cost — see ADR-001 + parse-pool.ts),\nretained for the future huge-file case. Ignored when `parallel === false`.\n- `serial` (`parallel === false`): the original in-order loop. Used by incremental `crib update`\n(1-3 changed files), determinism cross-checks, and custom-extractor runs (workers can't receive\nclass instances).\n`defaultRegistry` flags that the registry came from `defaultExtractors()` (no custom\n`opts.extractors`) — the worker pool only ships the default fleet. The concurrency + serial paths\nhonor any registry. `diagnosticLimit` bounds the retained diagnostics array (counts stay full)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts@L48","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":48,"end":50}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":48,"end":50},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2106881c98ed4cd37fbb7b1bc7feee9b68656c6a889cdacd509307235a7f8133","meta":{"text":"A per-file extraction outcome retained for diagnostic aggregation. The serial, concurrent, and\nworker paths each collect these in DISCOVERY order, then fold them through\n{@link aggregateDiagnostics} so the diagnostics surface is identical across modes."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts@L56","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":56,"end":56}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":56,"end":56},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:c7d44bfb4d02fe523da5f5bea7706b4766ac26e51be2af14658930f1eef35f9b","meta":{"text":"An empty ParseStats (zeroed counts, empty aggregations) for the noop / fallback paths."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts@L70","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":70,"end":76}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/parse.ts","span":{"start":70,"end":76},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:e0a797f0876a1d3794e087b93002dd1d920185005adb64fb42a74f2d14606f9e","meta":{"text":"Aggregate per-file diagnostics (in DISCOVERY order) into the `ParseStats` diagnostics fields.\nCounts EVERY diagnostic in `byCode`/`bySeverity`/`byExtractor` (never bounded — the summary is\nalways complete), while the `diagnostics` array retains only the first `limit` records in\ndiscovery order; the remainder is reported in `diagnosticsTruncated`. Pure + deterministic: same\ninput ⇒ same output, so serial / concurrent / worker modes produce identical diagnostics."}}
